# Ship the extension, not the repository.
#
# An allow-list rather than a deny-list, because the deny-list this
# replaced shipped every workflow, every tools/ script,
# .pre-commit-config.yaml, .github/actionlint.yaml, AGENTS.md,
# ARCHITECTURE.md, PUSH-AUDIT.md, REVIEWS.md, RELEASE-SETUP.md,
# renovate.json and biome.json to every user: 24 of the 27 packaged
# files were repository infrastructure rather than the extension.
# Phase 7 is the phase that makes the .vsix public, so it is the phase
# that has to decide what is in it.
#
# The consequence to know about: a new file has to be named here to
# reach a user. That is the point -- the failure mode of a deny-list is
# silent, and this one's was.
**

!package.json
!README.md
!LICENSE
!out/src/*.js

# Note the allow rule is *.js, not out/src/**. A trailing "**/*.map"
# deny does NOT override an earlier "!" allow in vsce's matcher -- it
# was tried, and the maps shipped anyway. Naming only the .js is what
# actually keeps them out, and a map is useless here regardless, since
# the .ts sources it points at are not in the package.
